                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The air tightness of your home could be increased by the replacement of the weather stripping on all doors and windows. Increasing the air tightness will contribute to reduce the energy consumption and the heat loss through the envelope.



</airSeal>
                <ceilingsCathedral>After inspection there is room to add more insulation. In this moment your roof insulation is composed by 2 layers of 6'' of batt insulation for a r value of R-40. You can add an additional 6'' (R-20) to reach an insulation level of R-60 or even   R-70 with the addition of 10'' instead of 6'' of insulation.



The addition of insulation will contribute to keep the heat inside the heated space during the heating season. On the opposite in summer it will increase the resistance against the heat on the roof the overheating the 2nd floor.



During the infiltration we've found some air leaks from the attic hatch. The installation of weather strips can help to sealed it.

</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>The foundation is not insulated. Only the pony wall is insulated, but not on the entire perimeter. We suggest to add the insulation on the rest of the uninsulated perimeter.

Concerning the concrete wall, we suggest the installation of material like rigid insulation to protect the interior space against the thermal bridge.

Thermal bridging is the passage of cold through condution from outside to inside. This situation coud result in condensation against the walls. 

We suggest the usage of an insulation and vapour barrier material. The vapour barrier is a very important component to be on the warm side to stop the humidity to hit the cold surface and condense. This situation can lead to  formation of mould and affect human health and the air quality of your home.</foundation>
                <windows>The actual windows are the original. We recommend the installation of new windows to increase the efficiency of your home and reduce the heat loss through the windows. The new units must respect the following:



- ENERGY STAR

- ZONE 3

- TRIPLE GLASS

- ARGON 

- LOW-E

</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>Your home is not equipped with a ventilation system. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI certified (Home Ventilating Institute) and certified ENERGY STAR.



The installation of this type of equipment can contribute to increase the air quality of your home. With the presence of a ducting system for the furnace, the ventilation unit can be connected to the ducts.</VentilationSystem>
                <WaterConservation>The replacement of the existing toilet for a low flow toilet can contribute to the reduction of water consumption.</WaterConservation>
            </RURComments>
